<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan sells two fuel oil cargoes at under 104/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan sells two fuel oil cargoes at under 104/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has sold by tender two 30,000-tonne cargoes of 3.0-percent sulphur, 180-centistoke fuel oil at just under $104 per tonne, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>The cargoes were awarded to a Dutch trader and a Singapore trader, they said. The cargo is for September 11-20 lifting on a free-on-board Kaoshiung basis.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold one 30,000-tonne cargo of 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil at around $100 per tonne for August 4-8 lifting, fob basis.</p>
